Now I have a clear picture. Let me understand the bug:

The `render()` function in `app.js` keys off todo titles to match existing DOM elements:

```javascript
var existing = {};
for (var i = 0; i < todoList.children.length; i++) {
  var li = todoList.children[i];
  var label = li.querySelector('label');
  if (label) {
    existing[label.textContent.trim()] = li;
  }
}
```

Then it iterates the `todos` array (which is in model order) and for each todo, it either finds the existing element by title (and updates it) or creates a new one and appends it to the end. When a title changes (editing), the old title key no longer matches, so a new `<li>` is created and appended to the end, while the old `<li>` stays in place (keyed by the old title) and gets cleaned up later as a stale entry.

Wait, let me trace through more carefully:

1. Suppose todos = [{title: "one"}, {title: "two"}, {title: "three"}]
2. First render: creates 3 `<li>` elements, appended in order. existing = {"one": li1, "two": li2, "three": li3}
3. User edits "two" to "two edited"
4. `editTodo("two", "two edited")` updates `todos[1].title = "two edited"` and calls `render()`
5. In render:
   - existing = {"one": li1, "two": li2, "three": li3} (keyed by old title "two")
   - currentTitles = {"one": true, "two edited": true, "three": true}
   - "two" is NOT in currentTitles, so existing["two"] (li2, with label "two") is removed from DOM
   - Now iterate todos: 
     - "one" -> existing["one"] = li1, found, update in place
     - "two edited" -> existing["two edited"] = undefined, so create new li and `appendChild` to end
     - "three" -> existing["three"] = li3, found, update in place

So the order becomes: li1 (one), li3 (three), new-li (two edited). 

The bug is confirmed. The fix suggested: render by a stable per-todo id instead of by title.

Now my task as Captain is to:
1. Add the scenario to `features/todo-editing.feature`
2. Put it on the watchbill
3. STOP - do not write production code or step definitions

Let me look at what step definitions exist to understand what I can use in the scenario.

